.TH SCHNET 1
.SH NAME
schnet \- write the netlist of a schematic sheet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schnet
[
.B \-L
.I lib
] ...
.I sheet.sch
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Schnet
reads a schematic source,
.IR sch (5),
every page of it, and its symbols as
.IR schdraw (1)
does, and writes its flat netlist,
.IR netlist (5),
on the standard output: a part record for each part, by its
designator, with its type, values, part number and name (the path of
its groups and its own name, the page's first, as
.BR outputs.ch1.gain.rf ),
and a net record for each net, with its pins by their numbers.
A net named by a flag or by a port of the sheet is marked global, and
is one net over all the pages it is on.
Flags are not parts; each pin on no net is a pin record after the
nets, nc if an nc statement leaves it unconnected on purpose, \- if not,
for
.IR schcheck (1).
The output of a source is always the same: the parts and the pins of a
net are sorted by designator and pin, the nets by name.
.PP
The designators come from the number of the page, its place in the
file: R401 is the first resistor of the fourth page, counted by columns
from the left and down each column.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
schnet sheet.sch > sheet.nl && netdiff sheet.nl before.nl
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
sch(5), netlist(5), netdiff(1), schcheck(1), schdraw(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
FILE:LINE: and the fault, one a line; the netlist leaves out what a
fault touches.
Exit status 1 on any fault.
